>I am playing pc-hack 3.51 and have found that if I polymorph lets say 20 
>darts  I will eventually get 20 long swords or 20 maces.  I can then wield 
>all of these maces or long swords.  

I wonder if you could wield 20 Excaliburs...  This sure sounds like a bug!

>This is the only case where hack allows you to wield more than one weapon.  

Well, I'm not familiar with pc-hack, but on unix nethack it's possible to
wield multiple daggers, and I believe spears & darts too.

>Is this usefull,  does it make your 
>hitting power better does it add up all the +'s of the weapons together?
>
That would be pretty cool if it did (imagine wielding 20 +7 Excaliburs and
polymorphing into a marilith!!!!!) but when I wield multiple daggers, 
judging by the number of hits it takes to kill monsters (again, this is on
unix nethack) I'd say that it only counts as one weapon of that type.

BTW, how about as an added feature to any features a blessed wand of polymorph
might already have, suppose if when you zapped an item with it it could poly-
morph into something outside its class--e.g. a weapon could become food, etc.
Alternatively, how about when you zap something with a blessed wand of poly-
morph it stayed in the same item class, but you could select what type of item
you wanted (provided you had encountered it before, like with writing scrolls).
For example you could zap a dagger and have it become, at your command, a two-
handed sword.  Of course enchantments would never go up and gems & artifacts
would probably have to be excluded.
